  <!-- ===================== PHONIX ===================== -->
  <article class="sheet" id="phonix">
    <header>
      <h2>Phonix: AI-powered Phonics App</h2>
      <p>A team project from the MIT FutureMakers Program that uses AI-powered MadLibs and flashcards, with a gamified approach, to combat teen illiteracy.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <ul>
          <li>Helped develop the app as part of a team.</li>
          <li>Conducted outreach to K-12 teachers about classroom learning through social media.</li>
          <li>Finalist in the program’s Create-a-thon.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top:1rem">Phonix was compared against ABCmouse, Starfall, Reading.com, and Flocabulary on learner targeting, AI-powered feedback, gamified learning, personalized content, and accessibility and pricing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gallery">
        <figure class="zoomable s2 logo-tile"><button class="zoom" type="button"><img src="projects/phonix-app/images/logo.png" width="386" height="172" loading="lazy" alt="Phonix logo: a navy bird forming the letter P, with the word honix"></button><figcaption>Phonix logo</figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="zoomable s4 diagram"><button class="zoom" type="button"><img src="projects/phonix-app/images/competitive-analysis.png" width="778" height="446" loading="lazy" alt="Competitive analysis table comparing Phonix with four other apps across five features; Phonix has a check in every row"></button><figcaption>Competitive analysis</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
    <dl class="titleblock">
      <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Team member: development and teacher outreach</dd></div>
